@if (IsOpen)
{
    <div class="changelog-backdrop" @onclick="OnClose">
        <div class="changelog-modal" @onclick:stopPropagation="true">
            <div class="changelog-header">
                <div>
                    <div class="modal-title">Changelog</div>
                    <div class="changelog-version">Version @AppVersion</div>
                </div>
                <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-secondary" @onclick="OnClose">Close</button>
            </div>
            <div class="changelog-body">
                <div class="changelog-section">
                    <h4>Version 2.0.0</h4>
                    <div class="changelog-section">
                        <h6>New Features</h6>
                        <ul>
                            <li><strong>Undo and redo.</strong> Use the Undo and Redo buttons (also in the game
                                editor), or press <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>Z</kbd> to undo and <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>Y</kbd>
                                or <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>Shift</kbd>+<kbd>Z</kbd> to redo (<kbd>Cmd</kbd> on macOS).
                                Typing in one field counts as a single step, and the last 100 steps are kept. Undoing
                                back to your last save clears the "Unsaved changes" badge.
                            </li>
                            <li><strong>Drag and drop.</strong> Drag the grip next to a folder or cheat to reorder it,
                                or drop a cheat on a folder to move it inside. Game tiles can be dragged to reorder
                                games. It works with a mouse, touch, or pen, and with the keyboard: focus a grip and
                                use the arrow keys.
                            </li>
                            <li><strong>Sorting.</strong> Sort a folder or the top level A–Z (folders first), or sort
                                all games A–Z. A cheat can also be moved with the "Move cheat to…" list.
                            </li>
                            <li><strong>XML import and export.</strong> Export the open file as codelist XML, the
                                format used by melonDS-style tools, or import one. Exports also include enabled states,
                                One Hot, and master codes, so they import back into R4Everyone without losing anything.
                                Importing replaces the open file, and duplicate games in the XML are merged.
                            </li>
                            <li><strong>Confirmations.</strong> R4Everyone now asks before removing a game, a cheat, or
                                a folder that has content (empty folders are removed straight away), and before New,
                                Open, or Import discards unsaved changes.
                            </li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                    <div class="changelog-section">
                        <h6>General</h6>
                        <ul>
                            <li>R4Everyone now works on phones and tablets! The "Desktop required" screen has been
                                removed.
                            </li>
                            <li>On smaller screens, the File Controls and Actions panels become a toolbar above the
                                game grid.
                            </li>
                            <li>Errors are no longer silent. If a file can't be opened or saved, or a ROM can't be
                                read, you'll see a message explaining what went wrong.
                            </li>
                            <li>If something unexpected breaks, R4Everyone shows an error screen instead of
                                freezing. Your open file stays loaded.
                            </li>
                            <li>If cover art can't be loaded, a warning is shown instead of failing quietly.</li>
                            <li>Notifications have been restyled to match the rest of the app in light and dark mode.
                            </li>
                            <li>Files with a blank (<code>00 00 00 00</code>) or unrecognized encoding marker, which
                                some online cheat databases use, can now be opened. R4Everyone asks which encoding to
                                use (UTF-8, GBK, Big5, or Shift-JIS), and saving writes the corrected marker.
                            </li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                    <div class="changelog-section">
                        <h6>Editor</h6>
                        <ul>
                            <li>On phones, the game editor opens full-screen with <strong>Cheats</strong>,
                                <strong>Game</strong>, and <strong>Item</strong> tabs. Selecting a folder or cheat
                                switches to the Item tab automatically.
                            </li>
                            <li>Clicking a selected folder or cheat again now selects the game, instead of leaving
                                game details uneditable.
                            </li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                    <div class="changelog-section">
                        <h6>Fixes</h6>
                        <ul>
                            <li>New files are now saved as <code>cheats.dat</code> instead of <code>(new)</code>.</li>
                            <li>Calculating the Game ID and Checksum from a ROM now always reads the full header,
                                fixing occasional incorrect checksums.
                            </li>
                            <li>Turning off One Hot no longer disables cheats in the folder.</li>
                            <li>A game's checksum is now required. Games without one are flagged by the validator,
                                instead of the file failing with an error when you try to save.
                            </li>
                            <li>Games without cover art no longer show a loading bar for 10 seconds.</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="changelog-section">
                    <h4>Version 1.2.0</h4>
                    <div class="changelog-section">
                        <h6>Editor</h6>
                        <ul>
                            <li>Added Cheat Code Activator support. Users may now configure button states to activate
                                cheats.
                            </li>
                            <li>Activator supports an "Action Replay-Compatible" mode, which uses the IPC region's
                                <code>0x027FFFA8</code> offset for the X and Y buttons. This should almost always be
                                left
                                disabled unless users know they need it (Or if a code includes it).
                            </li>
                            <li>If a code includes an activator, a banner will be displayed above the Codes section.
                            </li>
                            <li>Adding an Activator will append a <code>D2000000 00000000</code> to the end of the code.
                                This is "standard" for Action Replay cheats, but it <em>does</em>
                                have the potential to affect codes. If this is a problem for a cheat you use, please
                                open an issue on GitHub!
                            </li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                    <div class="changelog-section">
                        <h6><code>R4Everyone.Binary4Everyone</code> Library</h6>
                        <ul>
                            <li>Added support for reading and writing <code>Activator</code>s in <code>R4Game</code>.
                            </li>
                            <li><code>Activator</code>s are not serialized or deserialized normally. Rather, they are
                                helper methods for modifying the underlying code.
                            </li>
                            <li>When adding <code>Activator</code>s, the library will automatically add
                                <code>D2000000 00000000</code> to the end of the code. You can avoid this by using
                                <code>R4Game.BuildCheatCodeWithActivator</code> instead and removing the final two
                                objects in the Code list.
                            </li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="changelog-section">
                    <h4>Version 1.1.0</h4>
                    <div class="changelog-section">
                        <h6>General</h6>
                        <ul>
                            <li>Redesigned R4Everyone, which now uses a grid layout instead of a simple tree view</li>
                            <li>The game grid will attempt to load cover art from GameTDB (Which is why the app takes a
                                few seconds to load, it must pre-process the GameTDB database).
                            </li>
                            <li>If cover art cannot be downloaded, a placeholder will be used instead.</li>
                            <li>Art will not be loaded until the game intersects the viewport.</li>
                            <li>R4Everyone now has a dark mode, and will remember your selection!</li>
                            <li>R4Everyone can now handle larger files due to lazy parsing. Games are not parsed until
                                selected. On save, the app recalculates everything before writing the file.
                            </li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>

                    <div class="changelog-section">
                        <h6>Editor</h6>
                        <ul>
                            <li>Master code editor has been redesigned to be 2 rows of 4-byte text fields instead of 8
                                individual rows.
                            </li>
                            <li>Cheat code editor has been completely overhauled to be a single Text Field instead of
                                multiple "rows" of text fields.
                            </li>
                            <li>The cheat code editor will now self-format when typing, and blocks non-hexadecimal
                                characters from being entered.
                            </li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                    <div class="changelog-section">
                        <h6>Notes</h6>
                        <ul>
                            <li>This changelog will appear on the first run of the app only, and will not appear again
                                unless the app is updated.
                            </li>
                            <li>Click the logo in the header to view it anytime.</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
}

@code {
    [Parameter] public bool IsOpen { get; set; }
    [Parameter] public string AppVersion { get; set; } = "1.0.0";
    [Parameter] public EventCallback OnClose { get; set; }
}
